Chapter: BitOpsArm
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect

 The positive arm for the bit lowering. Before it existed the corpus could not
 spell a bit operation at all: not one kernel in the tree uses `bit-and` or its
 siblings, so every sweep over the shaders was green about a capability that
 was absent (L-CONSTRUCT). This chapter is the input shape that was missing.

 What the emitted WGSL must contain, from docs/Reference/WgslSpec.md 8.10:

   bit-and    (a & b)
   bit-or     (a | b)
   bit-xor    (a ^ b)
   bit-not    (~a)
   bit-shl    (a << (u32(b) & 31u))          the count is u32, not i32
   bit-shr    (a >> (u32(b) & 31u))          arithmetic, sign propagating
   bit-shru   bitcast<i32>(bitcast<u32>(a) >> (u32(b) & 31u))

 The last two are the pair that matters: WGSL's >> on a signed operand is
 arithmetic, so bit-shr and bit-shru are the SAME token in WGSL and differ only
 in the round trip through u32. An emitter that lowered both to >> would pass
 every validator and be wrong for exactly the negative inputs a hash produces.

 We say:

Section: Field Extraction

  ba-red : Integer -> Integer
  ba-red (c) = bit-and (bit-shru c 16) 255

  ba-green : Integer -> Integer
  ba-green (c) = bit-and (bit-shru c 8) 255

  ba-blue : Integer -> Integer
  ba-blue (c) = bit-and c 255

  ba-pack : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ba-pack (r) (g) (b) = bit-or (bit-shl r 16) (bit-or (bit-shl g 8) b)

Section: Signed Shifts

 ba-arith keeps the sign and ba-logical does not, which is the whole
 distinction the lowering has to preserve.

  ba-arith : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ba-arith (v) (n) = bit-shr v n

  ba-logical : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ba-logical (v) (n) = bit-shru v n

  ba-mix : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ba-mix (a) (b) = bit-xor a (bit-not b)

Section: Kernel

  bitops-step : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  bitops-step (inb) (outb) (gid) = act
    c <- device-load inb gid
    device-store outb gid (ba-pack (ba-blue c) (ba-mix (ba-red c) (ba-arith c 3)) (ba-logical (ba-green c) 2))
  end

